"""Reviewed recurring TASK, separate from numerical schemas and population."""

MEASUREMENT_COMPARISON_TASK = 'Determine whether the selected experimental estimates measure the same activity of the studied molecule under sufficiently comparable conditions to assess agreement. Start with the supplied source material and the actual measurements received; a candidate annotation is not required. Identify the organism, genotype, molecular construct, preparation, partners and experimental system of each estimate. Establish whether compared molecules coexist or replace one another. Preserve separate constructs, purification/reconstitution states and unreported preparation identities.\n\nFor each estimate, identify what was directly detected and what quantity was inferred. Retain the endpoint, its sign, units, denominator, time window, fit or averaging basis, and whether a reported value is rounded, approximate, bounded or censored. An identical unit does not establish an identical estimand. Saturation turnover, rate under fixed substrate conditions, terminal conversion, affinity and reporter response can have different meanings. If different detected species can be expressed as one reaction flux, identify the reaction direction, stoichiometric coefficients and experimental support for that conversion; do not silently divide by an assumed coefficient.\n\nAssess comparability outside the intended change separately from effect isolation. Establish the intended difference and any additional changes in substrate concentration, partner abundance, redox state, regeneration system, temperature, pH, enzyme preparation or denominator. Determine whether the protocols support an estimate of one common-condition quantity, merely a comparison of source protocols, or complementary information. Do not treat a change required by a detection method as harmless without examining its biochemical consequences.\n\nExamine each method’s validity for the particular endpoint. Identify interfering signals, incomplete reporter coupling, calibration and recovery measurements, controls, detection limits and unresolved error mechanisms. A positive control or a required-partner omission can establish activity dependence without estimating an additive background. Distinguish random variability from an identified systematic bias. A weak or biased quantitative estimate may retain useful evidence for existence or partner dependence. Do not upgrade or discard all assertions about the molecule together.\n\nIdentify the physical measurements underlying each estimate and comparison. Separate repeated representations, repeated time points, technical replicates, paired measurements and independent preparations. Different assay methods may share protein, standards or upstream corrections. Preserve what is known about shared inputs and covariance; different identifiers or different rows are not evidence of independence. Retain uncertainty labels, estimator meanings and sample hierarchy. A source SD, an unspecified error bar or an uncounted claim of repeated batches is not a known covariance of the selected estimates.\n\nSelect supported source spans and answer the declared aspect-specific relationship questions. Ask deterministic readers and calculators for the requested native values and eligible numerical comparisons. Preserve descriptive protocol comparisons separately from common-condition consistency results, and separately from conditional explanations of a discrepancy. Mark unknown and conflicting relationships explicitly. Do not infer a p-value, probability of function, universal reliability grade, target-transfer weight or annotation credit. A comparison, its ratio and its log are representations of one contribution; no additional evidence is created by calculating or reporting them.\n'

INTERPRETATION_QUESTIONS = (('construct', 'Are the selected estimates from the same actual molecular construct, an intended variant, or different molecules? Matching names alone do not establish identity.', ('same_construct_supported', 'intended_variant', 'different', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('preparation', 'Do the actual records establish one physical preparation or different preparations? Separate assay identifiers and equal values do not establish independent batches.', ('same_preparation_supported', 'different_preparations_supported', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('preparation_target', 'Do the preparations estimate one preparation quantity or a supported common population estimand? Preserve incompatible and unestablished sampling targets.', ('same_preparation_quantity', 'same_population_estimand_supported', 'incompatible', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('protocol', 'What changed besides the intended variable, including substrate and partner amounts, redox dynamics, regeneration, temperature, pH and denominator?', ('matched_except_intended_change', 'additional_differences', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('endpoint', 'Are the directly detected endpoints the same quantity, linked by supported fixed reaction coefficients and direction, complementary, or incompatible? Coupling does not establish unbiased rate equivalence.', ('same_quantity', 'fixed_reaction_conversion', 'complementary', 'incompatible', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('denominator', 'Do both estimates use the same actual normalization basis? Protein mass, total molecular amount and active molecular amount are distinct.', ('same_basis_supported', 'different', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('functional_bearing', 'Do both endpoints support the same quantitative assertion, only existence or partner dependence, or complementary assertions? Do not upgrade all assertions together.', ('same_quantitative_assertion', 'existence_only', 'partner_dependence_only', 'complementary', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('attribution', 'What isolates catalysis of the intended polypeptide or complex from other contributors? Optical signal decomposition does not establish molecular causal attribution.', ('isolated_supported', 'mixed_contributors_identified', 'unresolved', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('sampling', 'Which physical measurements are repeated, shared, paired or independently prepared? Caption repeats and serial timepoints are not independent preparations; covariance remains unknown unless measured.', ('repeated_representation', 'shared_physical_estimate', 'paired_observations_supported', 'independent_preparations_supported', 'independence_not_established', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('systematic_coverage', 'Which actual random or systematic error terms are included in the selected covariance? Known common random variance does not quantify an unidentified fixed bias.', ('included_in_selected_covariance', 'identified_unresolved', 'not_established', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('left_validity', 'Does the left method quantify its declared endpoint on the selected estimate scale, or does identified interference remain unresolved? Retain useful existence or dependence evidence.', ('endpoint_quantification_supported', 'identified_unresolved_interference', 'corrected_endpoint_supported', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('right_validity', 'Does the right method quantify its declared endpoint on the selected estimate scale, or does identified interference remain unresolved? Retain useful existence or dependence evidence.', ('endpoint_quantification_supported', 'identified_unresolved_interference', 'corrected_endpoint_supported', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('left_readout_isolation', 'Which species or contributions form the left detected signal, and what separates them? Keep readout isolation separate from attribution of chemistry to the molecule.', ('isolated_signal_supported', 'mixed_optical_contributions', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('right_readout_isolation', 'Which species or contributions form the right detected signal, and what separates them? Keep readout isolation separate from attribution of chemistry to the molecule.', ('isolated_signal_supported', 'mixed_optical_contributions', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('optical.estimate_scale_applicability', 'Does the signed raw optical relation apply to these exact fitted or averaged estimates? A nonlinear fit need not preserve a linear relation between raw rates.', ('supported', 'stipulated_sensitivity', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('optical.scenario', 'Are common-rate equality and linear-mixture applicability to the selected fitted-report scale each explicitly supported or stipulated? Missing actual nuisance measurements remain missing.', ('supported', 'stipulated_sensitivity', 'unknown', 'conflicting')), ('quantity.estimator_scale', 'What was directly measured and what parameter was inferred? Preserve time window, fit, averaging, rounding and the actual endpoint-specific unit definition.', ('direct_rate', 'fitted_asymptote', 'reported_mean', 'terminal_amount', 'parameter_estimate', 'unknown', 'conflicting')))
